musb: host: don't add the scatterlist offset twice in the first PIO TX packet

sg_mapping_iter.addr already includes the entry's offset. musb_ep_program() added
urb->sg->offset again, so the first packet (512 bytes) of a PIO scatter-gather write
with a nonzero offset was read from the wrong place: silently wrong data on the disk, or,
with a highmem page, an oops when the sum runs past the page (offset 0x800: mt5398_write_fifo
faulting at the start of the next, unmapped page). urb->actual_length is 0 here (a retry has a
non-NULL buf), so it goes too. Later packets (musb_host_tx) already use sg_miter.addr as it is.

--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_host.c
@@ -821,8 +821,7 @@
 					sg_miter_stop(&qh->sg_miter);
 					goto finish;
 				}
-				buf = qh->sg_miter.addr + urb->sg->offset +
-					urb->actual_length;
+				buf = qh->sg_miter.addr;
 				load_count = min_t(u32, load_count,
 						qh->sg_miter.length);
 				musb_write_fifo(hw_ep, load_count, buf);
